CXR_VQA_RESULT={"status": "completed", "observation": {"answer": "Based on the lateral chest X-ray provided, there appears to be **left base pulmonary atelectasis**.\n\nHere's why:\n\n*   **Increased opacity:** The left lung base appears denser (whiter) than the right lung base. This increased density suggests a consolidation or collapse of the lung tissue.\n*   **Possible cause:** Atelectasis is a common cause of this finding. It refers to the collapse of part or all of the lung. It can be caused by various factors, including airway obstruction, compression, or fluid accumulation.\n\nWhile I can't definitively rule out right base atelectasis without more information or comparison to prior images, the left base finding is more prominent and suggestive of atelectasis.\n\n**Disclaimer:** This interpretation is based solely on the provided image and should not be considered a definitive diagnosis. A complete evaluation requires clinical correlation and potentially additional imaging studies.\n", "model": "google/medgemma-4b-it", "revision": "290cda5eeccbee130f987c4ad74a59ae6f196408", "backend_input_tokens": 299, "backend_output_tokens": 186}, "derived_images": [], "backend_compute_seconds": 18.627386485924944, "cuda_peak_allocated_bytes_by_visible_device": [9942664192], "original_image": "../../../assets/eeea6398ff472c9394f52995490a7e5e85831d38ff941649699e4ae627597091.png", "raw_result_file": "[REDACTED]", "clinical_correctness_verified": false, "actual_model_events": [{"kind": "generate", "model_class": "Gemma3ForConditionalGeneration", "module": "transformers.models.gemma3.modeling_gemma3", "status": "completed", "utc": 1794254089.1287987, "elapsed_s": 8.873005660949275}], "cuda_visible_devices": "1", "adapter_revision": "cxr-vqa-existing-snapshot-binding-3"}
